    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Embraced in 1955 by Kasper von Aupfholme to help manage the overwhelming workload of Cairo's Tremere chantry, Hyapatia is a talented Egyptian archaeology student turned curatrix. When her sire departed to investigate a newly discovered temple in the Western Desert (the Shenouda Cache) and then went silent, Hyapatia was left to process the incoming relics alone &mdash; and grew obsessed with an item labeled Lot 14: an immaculately preserved canopic jar of strange white stone, sealed with hieroglyphs she slowly deciphered.</p><p>When the last glyph was translated, the jar opened to reveal only swirling mist and a soft, seductive voice claiming to be an imprisoned djinn of the Realm of Smokeless Fire. In truth, the jar imprisons the entombed essence of the Cairo Methuselah known as the Lord of the Dream Court, sealed away by the sorcerers of a fallen Setite temple. The entity is now slowly, patiently manipulating the smitten and increasingly obsessed Hyapatia toward its release, fostering her mistaken romantic fascination with it and her ambition to seize the chantry from the acting regent, Sylvia Kilver, once her sire is confirmed lost.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Project icy Tremere solidarity in public, but privately seethe with ambition and a growing, dangerous infatuation with the voice from Lot 14 that you believe only you can hear and understand.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Kasper von Aupfholme (missing in the Western Desert). Unknowingly manipulated by the imprisoned Lord of the Dream Court (a Setite-aligned Methuselah) sealed within the canopic jar Lot 14. Keeps extensive, incriminating notes on her interactions with the Shenouda Djinn that, read by an impartial party, would reveal the entity's true nature and possible weaknesses. Rival: Sylvia Kilver.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
